Subject: Reject incompatible struct assignments before reflection panics

The shared validator used by management-common inserts values into generated
Go structs. Equal reflect.Kind values do not make their types assignable:
for example, []string cannot be assigned to a named []byte field. Check the
converted value's actual assignability before Set, returning the existing
API error instead of panicking. Keep the preceding bool, binary and pointer
conversions and valid interface assignments.

Origin: SONiC shared-module correction exposed by the original util tests;
covered by those tests and overlay/util/sonic_assignability_test.go.
https://github.com/securely1g/sonic-bazel-registry/pull/214

--- a/util/reflect.go
+++ b/util/reflect.go
@@ -288,7 +288,9 @@
 		n = reflect.Zero(ft.Type)
 	}
 
-	if !isFieldTypeCompatible(ft, n) && !IsValueTypeCompatible(ft.Type, v) {
+	// The conversions above preserve supported YANG bool/binary and pointer values.
+	// Equal reflect.Kind alone does not make slices, maps or named types assignable.
+	if !n.Type().AssignableTo(ft.Type) {
 		return fmt.Errorf("cannot assign value %v (type %T) to struct field %s (type %v) in struct %T", fieldValue, fieldValue, fieldName, ft.Type, parentStruct)
 	}
 
